---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The dropWhile half of the locality guard (#971). `291` renamed every stateful
# pragma whose chain provably starts at a sequential source and ends at a
# terminal IN THIS BODY; anything still carrying the bare name could not be
# proved local, so its stream may have been handed in by a caller who made it
# parallel — `first(items.parallelStream())` — and the sticky `int[1]` latch it
# would fuse into races across ForkJoin workers.
#
# It is the twin of `226`'s result, with the trigger changed: that rule fires
# when a `parallel()` call is visible in the method, this one when locality
# could not be established at all. The two compose — `226`/`227` run first and
# take the visibly parallel chains, `291` marks the provably local remainder,
# and whatever is left over arrives here.
#
# Unlike distinct and skip, dropWhile carries a predicate, so the revert rebuilds
# the Φ.hone.lambda that `208` swallowed: the SAM is a Predicate (method `test`,
# interface `()Ljava/util/function/Predicate;`, lambda signature
# `(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z`, all constants here), the stream call is
# `java/util/stream/Stream.dropWhile`, and the bridge signature is recovered
# from the pragma's `bridge-input` as `(<bridge-input>)Z`. A primitive dropWhile
# reaches this rule in the same shape, because `211` has already boxed the
# stream and `233` renamed the pragma, so the object `Stream.dropWhile` this
# rebuilds is the correct call between the `Φ.hone.box` and `Φ.hone.unbox` that
# `602`/`603` lower back around it.
#
# `reverted ↦ Φ.true` stops `208` re-recognising the rebuilt lambda, so the
# 208 → 292 → 701 cycle cannot spin; `701` lowers it back to the invokedynamic
# it came from.
name: unlocal-reverts-dropwhile
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.dropWhile,
    opcode ↦ 𝑒-opcode,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-input ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    bridge-output ↦ 𝑒-bridge-output,
    accepted ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    returned ↦ 𝑒-returned,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    target ↦ ⟦
      handle ↦ 𝑒-target-handle,
      class ↦ 𝑒-target-class,
      method ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
      signature ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
      is-interface ↦ 𝑒-target-is-interface
    ⟧
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.lambda,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    method ↦ "test",
    interface ↦ "()Ljava/util/function/Predicate;",
    lambda-signature ↦ "(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z",
    bridge-signature ↦ 𝑒-bsig,
    static ↦ "true",
    opcode ↦ 𝑒-opcode,
    target ↦ ⟦
      handle ↦ 𝑒-target-handle,
      class ↦ 𝑒-target-class,
      method ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
      signature ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
      is-interface ↦ 𝑒-target-is-interface
    ⟧,
    stream ↦ ⟦
      class ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      method ↦ "dropWhile",
      signature ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Predicate;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;"
    ⟧,
    reverted ↦ Φ.true
  ⟧
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-bsig
    function: concat
    args: ['"("', 𝑒-bridge-input, '")Z"']
